goldendog-firewall (1.0.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix rules in any language but English: the rule dialog built the ufw
    command from the translated dropdown text ("ufw permitir ...",
    "ufw blockieren ..."), which ufw rejects. Dropdowns now carry the
    ufw keyword (allow/deny/reject, in/out, tcp/udp) and only show the
    translation.
  * German: complete the translation (Add, Delete, Edit, Save, Direction,
    Protocol, Reject, ...).

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@goldendoglinux.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:10:00 -0300

goldendog-firewall (1.0.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Default policy radios (Incoming/Outgoing) say "Allow" instead of
    "Accept" ("Permitir" in Spanish), matching ufw and the rule dialog.
  * Translate "Allow" in all languages (only Spanish had it, so the rule
    dialog showed it in English); drop the unused "Accept" string.

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@goldendoglinux.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0300

goldendog-firewall (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Load the real UFW state (/etc/ufw/ufw.conf, /etc/default/ufw) on
    startup instead of a hardcoded "off" switch and default policies.
    Previously, saving a new rule on an active firewall disabled it.
  * Show "Status: active/inactive" under the firewall switch.

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@goldendoglinux.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300

goldendog-firewall (1.0.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Wayland taskbar icon association by installing desktop file as
    org.goldendoglinux.firewall.desktop (matching application_id).
  * Install firewall icon in /usr/share/icons/scalable/apps in addition to
    hicolor path for compatibility.

